# Stray workspace artefacts — files a mistyped shell command drops in the
# working directory, e.g. `PR description`, `adds foo`, `setup-rebase`, `ter`.
#
# ANCHORED TO THE REPOSITORY ROOT, deliberately. These were `**/`-prefixed,
# which made them match by BASENAME at any depth, and several of the patterns
# are ordinary source-file names:
#
#   **/setup*           ignored tests/vitest/setup.js — the vitest harness —
#                       and needed two `!` negations to undo itself. That
#                       tracked-but-ignored pair is what gate-29 reports.
#   **/update*Settings* would ignore an `updateSettings.js` store action.
#   **/*Analysis*       would ignore a `SecretAnalysisService.php`.
#   **/*encoding*       would ignore an `encoding.js`.
#   **/*references*     would ignore any `references.*`.
#
# None of those files exists yet, which is exactly why this was invisible: the
# rule does not break anything until someone adds a normally-named file, and
# then it silently fails to stage it. A stray artefact lands where the command
# was run — the repository root — so root-anchoring loses no coverage.
#
# The negations are gone with the rule that required them: `tests/vitest/setup.js`
# is no longer matched by anything, rather than being matched and re-allowed.
/PR *
/adds *
/implements *
/ALL *
/endpoints *
/ter
/clearCache*
/rebase*
/setup*

# Temporary test files that shouldn't be committed
simple-solr-test.php
test-solr-connection.php

phpqa/

# Docker AI models (too large for git)
docker/dolphin/models/

# Issues folder should be tracked
!issues/
!issues/**

/docusaurus/node_modules/
/docusaurus/build/
/docusaurus/.docusaurus/
# Test screenshots — images generated by browser test commands (test-app, run-test-scenario)
# Only images are ignored; markdown reports and scenario files are kept in git.
test-results/**/*.png
test-results/**/*.jpg
test-results/**/*.jpeg
test-results/**/*.gif
test-results/**/*.webp
openspec/test-site-results/**/*.png
openspec/test-site-results/**/*.jpg
openspec/test-site-results/**/*.jpeg
openspec/test-site-results/**/*.gif
openspec/test-site-results/**/*.webp

# Playwright e2e runtime artefacts — never commit the cached session cookie
# (.auth/admin.json) or the generated reports/results.
/tests/e2e/.auth/
/tests/e2e/playwright-report/
/tests/e2e/test-results/
# The CI config (tests/e2e/playwright.config.ts) deliberately writes to the APP
# ROOT instead of tests/e2e/, because that is where the shared quality
# workflow's upload-artifact steps look: server/apps/<app>/playwright-report/
# and server/apps/<app>/test-results/. Hence these two extra, differently-rooted
# entries alongside the tests/e2e/ ones above.
/playwright-report/
/test-results/
/coverage-vitest/
/coverage/

# docs-site build artefacts (regenerated by npm; never track)
docs/node_modules/
docs/build/

RESTYLE-PLAN.md